  "transcript": "A sprig of mint repaired the air. Joseph Priestley burned a candle in a sealed jar until the flame died and no new flame would light. He slid in a sprig of mint and waited. Ten days later a candle burned bright in that same air. Somehow the little green plant had made the air good again.",
